  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::169522",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is shown to interact with multiple potassium channel subunits, including Kcna6, Kcnf1, and Kcna7, which all participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is ultimately linked to the participation of Kcnv2, a key component of the delayed rectifier potassium channel. The consistent evidence across three distinct paths suggests that Dalfampridine may modulate potassium channel function through a shared mechanism, potentially influencing Kcnv2 indirectly. The observed scores indicate a strong, reliable relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Dalfampridine in regulating potassium channel activity, which could have implications for its pharmacological effects and therapeutic applications.",
